Notes for the next release.

CachedRowSet is not supported.

Text from the database that starts with "<html>" is checked before it is
displayed in SsLabel, SsTable cells and the items of the combo boxes and
lists; see SsHtml. The default, a checker with Rules.MULTILINE, renders
HTML that only formats text. If the text has anything else, such as an image, a link or
a style, the text is displayed literally, markup and all, and a warning
is logged that names what is not allowed. An application that needs more
can allow it,
    Globals.setOption(SsHtml.class, SsHtmlChecker.get(Rules.MULTILINE.withElements("img").withAttributes("img@src")));
or go back to the old behaviour with SsHtml.pass(); setSsHtml() does it
for one component or one SsTable. See NOTES/SsHtml-design.md.

Tests: a quick run does a fraction of the slowest test cases, those that
mostly check the JDK's label renderer and image decoders, and the fuzz
tests. Full runs are the default and what CI does; set the property
seesaw.test.quick to true for quick local builds, see IDE_SETUP.md.

SsTable paste parses DATE, TIME and TIMESTAMP cells like the cell editor
does, see DateTime; for example a date can be 11/23/2026, 2026-11-23,
2026-1-5 or 20261123. Before, only yyyy-m-d was accepted for a date.
Text that is not a valid date/time is reported as a cell that was not
written; before, a TIME or TIMESTAMP cell was set to null. A timestamp
fraction can have 1 to 9 digits, as Timestamp.toString() makes, so a
copied timestamp can be pasted. A TIMESTAMP no longer takes an offset,
such as " -08:00", since it is a local date-time; before, such text
parsed but then set the cell to null.

The default SsTimestampField format, SsFormat.TIMESTAMP, is now
TIMESTAMP_YYYYMMDD_STROKE_HHMMSS, for example "2026-11-23 10:15:30".
Before, it was TIMESTAMP_YYYYMMDD_STROKE_HHMMSS_SSSZ, which showed
milliseconds and the JVM's offset; that text never validated, so the
field was marked as an error. TIMESTAMP_YYYYMMDD_STROKE_HHMMSS_SSSZ is
deprecated, not yet implemented. Editing a value with a fraction of a
second drops the fraction.

A component is decorated when it, or a panel holding it, is added to a
decorator panel. Before, a component bound before it was in the
decorator panel, as the demos do, showed no error until the next
decorate, such as a record change. A new SsTimeField is empty; before,
it was set to the current time. SsCurrencyField uses its editLocale
while editing, or the displayLocale if there is no editLocale; before,
editLocale was ignored.
